# External API

## What this is
A set of read-only endpoints that trusted external systems (like hub-os) can call to fetch company data. This allows founders/owners to view company data in their personal dashboard without the company database being shared.

## Authentication
External API routes use an API key — not a user session. The key is stored in the consumer's `.env` and validated on every request.

```typescript
// app/api/external/middleware.ts (or at top of each external route)
const apiKey = req.headers.get('x-api-key')
if (!apiKey || apiKey !== process.env.EXTERNAL_API_KEY) {
  return Response.json({ error: 'Unauthorized' }, { status: 401 })
}
```

The `EXTERNAL_API_KEY` is generated once, stored in this system's `.env`, and shared with the external consumer's `.env`. Rotate it if compromised.

## Endpoints live under `app/api/external/`

```
app/api/external/
  brand-context/route.ts    ← GET brand context for an org
  outputs/route.ts          ← GET recent outputs for an org
  team/route.ts             ← GET team member list (names/roles only)
```

Never mix external API routes with internal routes. External routes always live under `app/api/external/`.

## Hard rules

### Read-only
External API endpoints must only serve GET requests. No POST, PATCH, PUT, DELETE. No mutations of any kind. The external consumer can view company data but never modify it.

```typescript
// ❌ NEVER in an external route
export async function POST(req: Request) { ... }

// ✅ ONLY
export async function GET(req: Request) { ... }
```

### Scoped response
Only return fields the external consumer needs to display. Never return full database rows, internal IDs that aren't needed, or sensitive fields.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — returns everything
const { data } = await supabase.from('brand_context').select('*')

// ✅ GOOD — only what's needed for display
const { data } = await supabase
  .from('brand_context')
  .select('voice, tone, pillars, target_audience')
  .eq('organization_id', orgId)
  .single()
```

### No user data
External endpoints never return individual user emails, passwords, session data, or personal information. Team endpoints return names and roles only.

### Rate limiting
External endpoints should include basic rate limiting. Even trusted consumers shouldn't be able to hammer the API.

## Adding a new external endpoint
1. Create under `app/api/external/<feature>/route.ts`
2. Validate API key at the top
3. GET only — reject all other methods
4. Select only the fields needed for display
5. Document what the endpoint returns in this rule or in `docs/`
